From: Jakub Jelen <jjelen@redhat.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 21:20:34 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] Update the upstream signing key

Refresh victortoso-E37A484F.keyring from keyservers: same
certificate(s), with self-signatures our copy was missing.
The commands are in the comment above its Source line.
victortoso-E37A484F.keyring was in the lookaside cache, which a pull
request cannot update, so it moves into git (dropped from sources).

The current key is needed to verify the release signature with
openpgpverify (sqv), which checks that the key was valid when the
release was signed.

Assisted-by: Claude Opus 5.5
